{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The elder of his house.</b> Because he is joined and attached to him — זְקַן." "<b>Under my thigh.</b> Because the one taking an oath must hold in his hand an object of a commandment, such as a Torah scroll or tefillin (Shevuot 38), and circumcision was his first commandment and came to him through pain, and it was cherished by him, so he took hold of it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:05.886206691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}